## Model card (unresolved — no distinct SKU)

- **Name:** GLM 5.2 Coding (as scaffolded)
- **Short description:** The dataset entry `glm-5.2-coding` (`opencode/glm-5.2-coding`) is a **coding-positioned framing of GLM-5.2**, not a separate published model. The curated meta itself states "**no separate 'GLM-5.2-Coding' SKU is published on Z.ai, Zen, OpenRouter or models.dev**" and that "**the coding SKU itself is unverified: the published 'SWE-bench 78.7%' claim could not be found in any source.**" Z.ai's actual release is a single model — **"GLM-5.2: Built for Long-Horizon Tasks"** (June 16, 2026) — with high/max reasoning modes; there is no distinct "Coding" checkpoint, model card, or spec sheet.
- **Provider / access:** No `glm-5.2-coding` endpoint is documented on Z.ai, OpenCode Zen, OpenRouter, or models.dev. GLM-5.2 (the real model) is served on Z.ai / Zhipu's API and hosts, MIT-licensed.
- **Release / knowledge:** GLM-5.2 released **June 16, 2026** (superseded by GLM-5.3, Aug 14 2026). No separate "GLM-5.2-Coding" release exists.
- **IDs:** `opencode/glm-5.2-coding` (scaffold) — not a confirmed published SKU.
- **Context window:** meta says **1,000,000** (this is GLM-5.2's window, not a distinct coding SKU's).
- **Modalities:** meta says **Text in/out** (GLM-5.2's modality).
- **Pricing:** meta says **$1.40/$4.40** per 1M, $0.26 cached (GLM-5.2's pricing).
- **Architecture:** GLM-5.2 is an MIT-licensed MoE; no separate "Coding" architecture is published.

### Raw benchmarks found

> Every benchmark located resolves to **GLM-5.2 (base)**, not a distinct coding SKU.

- **Vals AI `zai_glm-5.2`:** "**#1 open-weight and #3 overall on SWE-bench Verified (82.80%)**, and **#1 open-weight on Terminal-Bench 2.1 (67.79%)**." → these are the meta's "SWE-bench 82.8% (Vals)" and "TB 2.1 67.8% (Vals)" — **GLM-5.2's** numbers.
- **Z.ai GLM-5.2 blog:** "**81.0** vs 63.5 on **Terminal-Bench [2.1]**" (vendor) → the meta's "TB 2.1 81.0% (vendor)" — **GLM-5.2's**.
- **AA tau2-bench 99.1%** → the meta's tool-orchestration claim — again **GLM-5.2's**, not a separate coding model's.
- Artificial Analysis: **`glm-5-2-coding` returns 404** (no distinct page). GLM-5.2 base is tracked, not a "Coding" variant.
- The meta's "**SWE-bench 78.7%**" claim: **could not be found in any source** (confirmed on my pass) — an unverifiable figure.

> Provenance / conclusion: there is **no first-party model card, no distinct published SKU, and no benchmark attributable to "GLM-5.2-Coding" as separate from GLM-5.2**. The distinguishing numbers (Vals SWE-bench Verified 82.80% #1-open-weight/#3-overall, Terminal-Bench 2.1 67.79%/81.0%, AA tau2-bench 99.1%) all belong to the **`glm-5.2`** sibling, which is its own queue entry and will carry the scored lineage. Scoring this folder would (a) reattribute a sibling's evidence to a phantom SKU and (b) double-count GLM-5.2 — both forbidden by the exclusion convention.
> Recommended curator resolution: either (a) **retire/park the `glm-5.2-coding` scaffold** and fold it into `glm-5.2`, or (b) if Z.ai ever ships a genuine distinct GLM-5.2-Coding checkpoint with its own model card + evaluations, re-point this slug to it and re-research independently (do **not** reuse GLM-5.2's numbers even though they share a family name).

